# Integration Resilience

- Hide provider SDKs behind ports and translate provider errors into stable internal categories.
- Every network call defines a timeout, cancellation behavior, retry policy, and maximum attempt budget.
- Retry only transient failures; never retry validation, authorization, duplicate, or permanent business failures.
- Use idempotency keys and durable deduplication for payment, webhook, inventory, notification, and queue operations.
- Do not hold database transactions open during external calls unless the design explicitly handles partial failure.
- Persist enough provider reference and status data to reconcile safely without storing secrets or unnecessary payloads.
- Use circuit breaking, rate limits, dead-letter handling, and alerting where failure volume can harm the system.
- Test timeout, malformed response, duplicate delivery, partial success, and provider outage behavior.
